WEBVTT

00:02:29.896 --> 00:02:32.106
the places where we are prone
to disagreement,

00:02:32.148 --> 00:02:34.692
say, politics and religion?

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.485
Well, as it turns out,

00:02:36.527 --> 00:02:39.071
not only does Wikipedia's
model work there,

00:02:39.113 --> 00:02:41.282
it actually works really well.

00:02:41.324 --> 00:02:43.242
Because in our normal lives,

00:02:43.284 --> 00:02:46.329
these contentious
conversations tend to erupt

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.291
over a disagreement
about what the truth actually is.

00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:52.835
But the people who write these articles,

00:02:52.877 --> 00:02:55.922
they're not focused on the truth.

00:02:55.963 --> 00:02:57.882
They're focused on something else,

00:02:57.924 --> 00:03:01.427
which is the best
of what we can know right now.